{"id":"b97e57a60826afa3","group":"73","path":"73/73-thm-work-space-complementation.md","title":"Immerman–Szelepcsényi Theorem","display":"thm-immerman-szelepcsenyi — Immerman–Szelepcsényi Theorem","type":"theorem","metadata":{"type":"theorem","book":"Automata Theory, Languages and Computation (Hopcroft, Ullman)","book_abbrev":"73","label":"73-thm-work-space-complementation","aliases":["73-thm-work-space-complementation","73-thm-immerman-szelepcsenyi"],"display":"thm-immerman-szelepcsenyi — Immerman–Szelepcsényi Theorem","depends_on":["[[73-df-nondeterministic-work-space]]","[[73-df-exact-work-space-construction]]"]},"metadataError":null,"renderWarnings":[],"properties":[{"key":"type","html":"theorem"},{"key":"book","html":"Automata Theory, Languages and Computation (Hopcroft, Ullman)"},{"key":"book_abbrev","html":"73"},{"key":"label","html":"73-thm-work-space-complementation"},{"key":"aliases","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>73-thm-work-space-complementation</span><span>73-thm-immerman-szelepcsenyi</span></div>"},{"key":"display","html":"thm-immerman-szelepcsenyi — Immerman–Szelepcsényi Theorem"},{"key":"depends_on","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-1\" data-note=\"5487b1bca12f6c5f\" href=\"?note=5487b1bca12f6c5f\" title=\"73-df-nondeterministic-work-space\">73-df-nondeterministic-work-space</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-2\" data-note=\"cadee7248274622b\" href=\"?note=cadee7248274622b\" title=\"73-df-exact-work-space-construction\">73-df-exact-work-space-construction</a></span></div>"}],"html":"\n<h2 id=\"Hypothesis\">[Hypothesis]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathsf{NSPACE}\">\\(\\mathsf{NSPACE}\\)</span> and <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathsf{coNSPACE}\">\\(\\mathsf{coNSPACE}\\)</span> (nondeterministic space and complement classes, see <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-3\" data-note=\"5487b1bca12f6c5f\" href=\"?note=5487b1bca12f6c5f\" title=\"73-df-nondeterministic-work-space\">73-df-nondeterministic-work-space</a>)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\operatorname{SpaceConstructible}\">\\(\\operatorname{SpaceConstructible}\\)</span> (full space constructibility)</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Assertion\">[Assertion]</h2>\n<figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{thm\\text{-}immerman\\text{-}szelepcsenyi}\\vdash\n\\forall s:\\mathbb N\\to\\mathbb N_{&gt;0}\\;\\Bigl(\n\\operatorname{SpaceConstructible}(s)\n\\land\\bigl(\\forall n\\in\\mathbb N\\;\n\\lceil\\log_2(n+2)\\rceil\\leq s(n)\\bigr)\n\\longrightarrow\n\\mathsf{NSPACE}(s)=\\mathsf{coNSPACE}(s)\n\\Bigr)\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{thm\\text{-}immerman\\text{-}szelepcsenyi}\\vdash\n\\forall s:\\mathbb N\\to\\mathbb N_{&gt;0}\\;\\Bigl(\n\\operatorname{SpaceConstructible}(s)\n\\land\\bigl(\\forall n\\in\\mathbb N\\;\n\\lceil\\log_2(n+2)\\rceil\\leq s(n)\\bigr)\n\\longrightarrow\n\\mathsf{NSPACE}(s)=\\mathsf{coNSPACE}(s)\n\\Bigr)\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><h2 id=\"Remark\">[Remark]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Inductive counting verifies the number of configurations reachable within successive path lengths while storing only a constant number of configurations and <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"O(s(n))\">\\(O(s(n))\\)</span>-bit counters. This recognizes nonreachability in the same asymptotic space.</li>\n<li>The original atom's 28 automata-and-grammar dependencies were unrelated; only nondeterministic space and its constructibility condition enter the theorem.</li>\n</ul>\n","headings":[{"id":"Hypothesis","text":"[Hypothesis]","level":2},{"id":"Assertion","text":"[Assertion]","level":2},{"id":"Remark","text":"[Remark]","level":2}],"links":[{"target":"73-df-nondeterministic-work-space","status":"resolved","id":"5487b1bca12f6c5f","anchor":"ref-1","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[73-df-nondeterministic-work-space]]","embed":false},{"target":"73-df-exact-work-space-construction","status":"resolved","id":"cadee7248274622b","anchor":"ref-2","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[73-df-exact-work-space-construction]]","embed":false},{"target":"73-df-nondeterministic-work-space","status":"resolved","id":"5487b1bca12f6c5f","anchor":"ref-3","targetAnchor":"","location":"正文","heading":"[Hypothesis]","excerpt":"$\\mathsf{NSPACE}$ and $\\mathsf{coNSPACE}$ (nondeterministic space and complement classes, see [[73-df-nondeterministic-work-space]])","embed":false}],"math":[{"tex":"\\mathsf{NSPACE}","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathsf{coNSPACE}","display":false},{"tex":"\\operatorname{SpaceConstructible}","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{thm\\text{-}immerman\\text{-}szelepcsenyi}\\vdash\n\\forall s:\\mathbb N\\to\\mathbb N_{>0}\\;\\Bigl(\n\\operatorname{SpaceConstructible}(s)\n\\land\\bigl(\\forall n\\in\\mathbb N\\;\n\\lceil\\log_2(n+2)\\rceil\\leq s(n)\\bigr)\n\\longrightarrow\n\\mathsf{NSPACE}(s)=\\mathsf{coNSPACE}(s)\n\\Bigr)","display":true},{"tex":"O(s(n))","display":false}],"bytes":1392,"backlinks":[{"id":"d828b0346ed8091f","anchor":"ref-2","locations":["元数据 · depends_on"],"count":1,"excerpt":""}],"outgoing":["5487b1bca12f6c5f","cadee7248274622b"]}